# lamp-update's own switches (#6607), read by lamp-update itself, never by systemd, once at its start: a round
# carries this file among the build's settings, so a lamp already in a home turns them on without its own unit,
# which no round rewrites, changing (docs/updates.md, "The update switch file"; docs/switches.md). A switch set
# in lamp-update.service's environment wins over this file, so `off` there holds it off. Anything but `on` is off.
LAMP_APP_ENGINES=on
LAMP_SKILL_TASKS=on
LAMP_SKILL_DEFAULT_AGENT=on
LAMP_SKILL_GATEWAY_RUNS=on
